  "limits": [
    "Conventional physical IOAPIC/MSI/MSI-X destinations are individual IDs 0..254. Physical x2APIC IPIs retain 32 bits and reject FFFFFFFF; FF is architecturally valid only for x2APIC IPIs.",
    "Full/high/sparse BSP and destination boundaries are actual-source host cases with mocked CPUID/MSR/register/online state, not native high-ID hardware qualification.",
    "The scoped sparse VM has six possible slots but exactly four present CPUs (IDs 0/2/4/6); only these four qualify and execute preemption/TLB/clock probes. The x2 option is a separate real-mode build, not a hardware fault injection.",
    "A paused QEMU preview refused high IDs outside its four possible slots before guest execution; it is not a failed OS boot or a high-ID runtime proof. Expanding possible slots is outside this bounded fixture/capacity claim.",
    "CPU slot recycling/hotplug, dynamic IRQ migration and interrupt remapping remain separate work. The BSP has one confirmed boot lifetime; AP authority uses its exact start epoch.",
    "No new Windows-host or native hardware acceptance. Exactly one final normal-artifact STANDARD; no stable speedup is inferred."
  ]
